---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getRegistry } from '../lib/registry';
const registry = getRegistry();
const count = registry.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.entries.length, 0);
---
<BaseLayout title="Agent Status Codes" description="A shared, machine-readable status vocabulary for agents and applications.">
  <main data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="home-hero shell">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Open protocol · ASC 0.1 experimental</p>
        <h1>Status codes for agents</h1>
        <p class="lede">HTTP status codes let a client act on a response without first learning the server's vocabulary. ASC gives agents and applications the same shared language.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/spec/registry/">Browse the registry</a>
          <a class="button" href="/spec/">Read ASC 0.1</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="envelope" aria-label="Example ASC status envelope">
        <div class="envelope-head"><span>STATUS ENVELOPE</span><span>JSON</span></div>
        <pre><code><span class="line">&#123;</span>
<span class="line">  "spec_version": <b>"0.1.0"</b>,</span>
<span class="line">  "status": &#123;</span>
<span class="line">    "code": <em>3002</em>,</span>
<span class="line">    "name": <b>"HUMAN_APPROVAL_REQUIRED"</b>,</span>
<span class="line">    "phase": <b>"WAITING"</b>,</span>
<span class="line">    "terminal": <i>false</i></span>
<span class="line">  &#125;,</span>
<span class="line">  "retry": &#123; "safe": <i>false</i> &#125;</span>
<span class="line">&#125;</span></code></pre>
        <figcaption>Transport success and agent outcome remain separate</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <nav class="home-classes shell" aria-label="Browse by code class">
      {registry.map((item) => <a href={`/spec/registry/#${item.anchor}`} style={`--class-color:${item.color}`}>
        <span>[{item.digit}xxx]</span><strong>{item.short}</strong>
      </a>)}
    </nav>

    <section class="home-intro shell">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The protocol</p>
        <h2>One vocabulary across agent boundaries</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Agent integrations often define their own terms for running, waiting for a person, partial success, policy refusal, and recovery. ASC defines portable meanings once so software can decide what to show and what to do next.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/why/">Why ASC exists <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="registry-preview shell">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">{count} assigned codes</p><h2>Enter the code space</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/spec/registry/">Open the full registry <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <div class="preview-grid">
        {registry.slice(0, 4).map((item) => <a href={`/spec/registry/#${item.anchor}`} style={`--class-color:${item.color}`}>
          <span>{item.digit}xxx</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.entries.length} assigned codes</p>
        </a>)}
        <a class="all-classes" href="/spec/registry/"><span>5xxx to 9xxx</span><h3>Failures, trust, operations, and extensions</h3><p>Continue through the registry</p></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
